set{―}{AD}$ are consecutive sides to $\\overset{―}{AB}.$" 13194139534885 17592186045417 true] [17592186442731 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442698 13194139534885 17592186045417 true] [17592186442731 1069 "q-117931" 13194139534885 17592186045417 true] [17592186442731 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534885 17592186045417 true] [17592186442731 1071 "![](images/db/dbcae9590b6112acefabbd50ded7e0b44c413c2e8d874613262f6fa53094f8c9.png)\n\nWhich sides are consecutive to $\\overset{―}{DE}?$" 13194139534885 17592186045417 true] [17592186442731 1072 #uuid "dd3ebc93-bf89-529b-97c7-60c59d0406c6" 13194139534885 17592186045417 true] [17592186442731 1074 "Two sides are consecutive if they have a vertex in common. Therefore, $\\overset{―}{CD}$ and $\\overset{―}{EF}$ are consecutive sides to $\\overset{―}{DE}.$" 13194139534885 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0101c798-7940-555f-9b8a-758b31da095c" 17592186442615 "answer-01a07b11-7e9a-5be9-bf1d-a9ddd09ad102" 17592186442616 "answer-0a8c94af-b4bf-5dab-8925-11756cd2cb59" 17592186442617 "answer-0b27b60d-8f6b-5319-8584-6b96b3c15ba8" 17592186442618 "answer-0e7c16e2-3f40-52fc-9124-1ce5e4f5bab1" 17592186442619 "answer-0f172ff4-b9f2-5351-bdfd-09f6036ebd62" 17592186442620 "answer-147ffaa5-9f87-51d3-b4df-b205a4cd4894" 17592186442621 "answer-159690ad-d0b6-5818-b534-17f8acc04e69" 17592186442622 "answer-18c308be-9e1e-56e2-ad5d-36847007c8f8" 17592186442623 "answer-19a70177-629a-598d-83d2-82d9bb6a9db1" 17592186442624 "answer-1b719cb0-bf3e-5422-9014-64963e98d617" 17592186442625 "answer-24a6a51f-ef39-5985-bb20-68feb5096f25" 17592186442626 "answer-2dfad3b8-82ab-5de4-8e98-222d1152b2c3" 17592186442627 "answer-2f5d5aff-dad6-5ecb-be8f-94ad8daa507d" 17592186442628 "answer-32035f88-4386-5a0e-9a90-12c39c00ba8d" 17592186442629 "answer-32da3b54-b750-5887-b04f-86b7ef454ce8" 17592186442630 "answer-349569f0-9441-5341-922f-65d8019d65d1" 17592186442631 "answer-3a749281-1cff-5ac0-8364-84c262625e80" 17592186442632 "answer-3e85c536-ba38-5d8c-901f-4e5bc71b071f" 17